2026, and promotions are excluded. QuickBooks also has a $0 Free plan for one user sending up to two invoices a month. Published Plans and Monthly List Prices Side by Side QuickBooks Online FreshBooks Free or lowest-priced plan Free: $0 for 1 user sending up to 2 invoices a month. Lite: $23 a month for invoicing up to 5 clients. Next paid plans Simple Start: $38 a month for 1 user. Essentials: $85 a month for up to 3 users. Plus: $43 a month for invoicing up to 50 clients. Higher published plans Plus: $140 a month for up to 5 users. Advanced: $340 a month for up to 25 users. Premium: $70 a month for unlimited clients. Plan limit used in the cost model The published user cap determines the cheapest eligible paid tier. The published billable-client cap determines the base tier. Additional users The modeled paid tier rises from $38 to $85 when a second user is needed, to $140 for a fourth user, and to $340 for a sixth. The model adds $11 a month for each user beyond the first on Lite, Plus or Premium. One user and 6 to 50 clients Simple Start: $38 a month. Plus: $43 a month. Three users and 51 or more clients Essentials: $85 a month. Premium plus two $11 Team Members: $92 a month. Plan outside the paid-price grid Free: $0, with its 1-user and 2-invoice monthly limits. Select: quote-based, with no public monthly price. 📣 Building in finance? Put your product in front of readers comparing options on this page. Advertise With Us → Our Takeaway for QuickBooks vs FreshBooks Choose by both user count and billable-client count if monthly list price is your deciding factor. FreshBooks is cheaper for two users at every client count in the model and for four to 25 users at every client count. For one user, FreshBooks Lite costs less through five clients, while QuickBooks Simple Start costs less from six clients onward. At exactly three users, FreshBooks costs less through 50 clients, then QuickBooks Essentials costs less from 51 clients onward. This price recommendation is not for someone whose decision depends on features, support or integrations. Compare the specific requirements you need instead of treating the cheaper modeled price as an overall product verdict. A change in either product's prices or plan caps, FreshBooks' $11 seat price, or a promotion could change the result. Count the people who need access and the clients you will invoice, then compare that pair of counts with the grid below. QuickBooks vs FreshBooks at a Glance For one user, the FreshBooks base price rises from $23 to $43 when the client count moves from five to six. QuickBooks Simple Start remains $38 in both cases, so the lower price switches from FreshBooks to QuickBooks. For three users, the next switch occurs between 50 and 51 clients. FreshBooks Plus with two added Team Members costs $65 through 50 clients. At 51 clients, Premium with those same two seats costs $92, above QuickBooks Essentials at $85. Two users never reach that QuickBooks advantage in the modeled range: FreshBooks Premium with one added seat is $81, below Essentials at $85. User count can reverse the result again. Four users require the $140 QuickBooks Plus tier in the model, while FreshBooks Premium with three added seats costs $103. Even at 25 users and more than 50 clients, modeled FreshBooks Premium costs $334 against QuickBooks Advanced at $340. These comparisons cover one to 25 users. They do not assign a QuickBooks price above its published 25-user cap. The $0 QuickBooks Free plan is a separate case. For one user who sends no more than two invoices a month, its price is below every paid plan in this comparison. The paid-plan grid excludes Free because its invoice limit is a separate constraint from user and client counts. Monthly Cost by Number of Users and Clients Our 49-case model prices the cheapest eligible paid QuickBooks tier against a FreshBooks plan selected by billable-client count. QuickBooks costs $38 for one user, $85 for two to three users, $140 for four to five users, and $340 for six to 25 users. FreshBooks starts at $23 for up to five clients, $43 for six to 50, or $70 for 51 or more. We then add $11 for each FreshBooks user beyond the first. The grid shows monthly list prices in dollars. QB means QuickBooks Online and FB means FreshBooks. It uses user counts of 1, 2, 3, 4, 5, 10 and 25 against client counts of 3, 5, 6, 20, 50, 51 and 100. The model excludes promotions, QuickBooks Free and quote-based FreshBooks Select. Users 3 clients 5 clients 6 clients 20 clients 50 clients 51 clients 100 clients 1 QB $38 / FB $23 QB $38 / FB $23 QB $38 / FB $43 QB $38 / FB $43 QB $38 / FB $43 QB $38 / FB $70 QB $38 / FB $70 2 QB $85 / FB $34 QB $85 / FB $34 QB $85 / FB $54 QB $85 / FB $54 QB $85 / FB $54 QB $85 / FB $81 QB $85 / FB $81 3 QB $85 / FB $45 QB $85 / FB $45 QB $85 / FB $65 QB $85 / FB $65 QB $85 / FB $65 QB $85 / FB $92 QB $85 / FB $92 4 QB $140 / FB $56 QB $140 / FB $56 QB $140 / FB $76 QB $140 / FB $76 QB $140 / FB $76 QB $140 / FB $103 QB $140 / FB $103 5 QB $140 / FB $67 QB $140 / FB $67 QB $140 / FB $87 QB $140 / FB $87 QB $140 / FB $87 QB $140 / FB $114 QB $140 / FB $114 10 QB $340 / FB $122 QB $340 / FB $122 QB $340 / FB $142 QB $340 / FB $142 QB $340 / FB $142 QB $340 / FB $169 QB $340 / FB $169 25 QB $340 / FB $287 QB $340 / FB $287 QB $340 / FB $307 QB $340 / FB $307 QB $340 / FB $307 QB $340 / FB $334 QB $340 / FB $334 At one user and five clients, the comparison is $23 for FreshBooks Lite against $38 for QuickBooks Simple Start. Adding one billable client moves FreshBooks to its $43 Plus tier. The extra client changes the price-only result even though the QuickBooks user count has not changed. At two users and 51 clients, FreshBooks costs $70 for Premium plus $11 for one added seat, or $81. QuickBooks Essentials costs $85. At three users and the same client count, the FreshBooks calculation becomes $70 plus two $11 seats, or $92. Essentials remains $85 because its published cap covers three users. That single added user changes which product costs less. The grid samples seven user counts, but the pricing rules also cover the counts between them. For six to 25 users, QuickBooks Advanced stays at $340 in this model. At 25 users and 51 or more clients, FreshBooks reaches $70 plus 24 seats at $11 each, or $334. That leaves FreshBooks $6 below Advanced at the largest published QuickBooks user count. The FreshBooks seat charge is a modeling assumption for every user beyond the first, so compare it with the seats you would need. What the Price Comparison Leaves Out The grid compares published monthly list prices, not what each product can do for a particular business. QuickBooks inputs are limited to plan prices and user caps, plus the Free plan's invoice limit. No QuickBooks feature, support or accountant-access claim is used to choose a winner. FreshBooks describes plans built around the number of clients you invoice. Lite covers invoices to five clients, expense tracking and estimates. Plus raises the invoice limit to 50 clients and lists proposals, client retainers, financial and accounting reports, receipt scanning and accountant access. Premium allows unlimited clients and lists project profitability. Those published details can help you identify a requirement, but the cost grid gives none of them a score. The FreshBooks base prices in the grid also exclude optional add-ons other than modeled Team Members. FreshBooks lists Advanced Payments at $20 a month and Payroll at $40 a month plus $6 a month per user. Neither charge appears in a grid cell. Select has no public monthly price and is excluded as well, so the table cannot decide whether a Select quote would cost less for a given team. Promotions are excluded from every modeled figure. If you intend to buy at an advertised discount, compare the amounts and terms shown on the QuickBooks pricing page and FreshBooks pricing page with the list-price result. A discount can change the price comparison for the period it applies. The grid does not assign a discounted price to either product. Features, support and integrations can also change which product you would choose, even when the list-price arithmetic stays the same. Identify any requirement that could outweigh the monthly difference before using a $5 gap, such as the one-user, six-client case, to make the decision. Who Should Pick QuickBooks or FreshBooks QuickBooks Online has the lower modeled paid price for a single user invoicing six or more clients. At six to 50 clients, Simple Start is $38 against FreshBooks Plus at $43. At 51 or more clients, Simple Start remains $38 while FreshBooks Premium is $70. A single user sending up to two invoices a month also has the separate $0 QuickBooks Free option. QuickBooks Essentials has one other lower-price case: exactly three users with 51 or more clients. Its $85 monthly list price is $7 below FreshBooks Premium with two added Team Members at $92. At 50 clients, FreshBooks Plus with those seats is $65, so count billable clients before applying the three-user result. FreshBooks has the lower modeled paid price for a one-user business invoicing up to five clients. It also costs less for every modeled client count with two users and with four to 25 users. The margin varies. With two users and 51 or more clients, FreshBooks is $81 against QuickBooks at $85. With four users and that client count, FreshBooks is $103 against QuickBooks at $140. A reader who needs a feature, support arrangement or integration that this price model does not score should not choose solely from these figures. Write down that requirement and assess it separately. If the decision is limited to sending invoices, the invoicing apps for freelancers roundup offers a different comparison. If neither product fits the price or requirements you have identified, consider other QuickBooks alternatives . This answer would change if either published plan price or cap changes, if FreshBooks changes its $11 Team Members charge, or if a promotion changes the amount you would pay. For a quickbooks vs freshbooks price decision, count your users and billable clients, find the matching grid cell, and verify today's figures on the QuickBooks pricing page and FreshBooks pricing page. Frequently asked questions Is QuickBooks or FreshBooks cheaper for a freelancer? For one user on paid plans, FreshBooks Lite costs less with up to five billable clients: $23 a month against QuickBooks Simple Start at $38. From six clients onward, QuickBooks Simple Start has the lower modeled list price. If one user sends up to two invoices a month, QuickBooks Free costs $0. What is comparable to QuickBooks? FreshBooks is an option to compare with QuickBooks Online when choosing by monthly list price, user count and billable-client count. The QuickBooks alternatives roundup covers more products if you want a wider list. What is FreshBooks accounting software? FreshBooks offers invoicing and expense tracking, with plan limits based on how many clients you invoice. Its published plans also list estimates, proposals, projects and reports, with the available features varying by plan. Is there a free QuickBooks plan? Yes. QuickBooks Online lists a Free plan at $0 for one user sending up to two invoices a month. The paid-price grid does not include that invoice-limited plan. How much does adding a team member cost? FreshBooks lists Team Members at $11 a month per additional user on Lite, Plus and Premium. In this model, QuickBooks instead moves to the cheapest paid tier with enough user capacity: $38 for one user, $85 for two to three, $140 for four to five, or $340 for six to 25. Do promotions change the answer? They can change the amount you pay and may change which product costs less during a discount period. Every comparison here uses monthly list prices with promotions excluded. Compare any current offer on the QuickBooks pricing page and FreshBooks pricing page. Free calculators to help you decide Self-Employment Tax Calculator →